# Cursor Rules for Brasil Global Marketing Machine

## Project Context
- Next.js 15 App Router + React 19 + TypeScript 5.6+ + Tailwind CSS v4
- Marketing machine for "Brasil Global" — content engine for Brazilians abroad
- 8-layer architecture: intelligence, strategy, content-engine, visual-factory, canvas, studio, publisher, ads-manager, analytics, community

## Code Style
- Max 150 lines per page/component, 40 per utility, 150 per hook, 100 per server action
- Zero `any`. Use `unknown` + narrowing.
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Extract shared logic to `src/shared/`
- Config centralization in `src/config/`

## AI Provider Usage
- **Premium copy**: Claude 3.7
- **Structured/JSON**: GPT-4.1
- **Budget/volume**: DeepSeek V3
- **Images**: FLUX 2 (fal.ai), Ideogram 3 (typography), Recraft V3 (vectors)
- **Video**: Pika (Reels), Kling 3.0 (B-roll), Runway Gen-4.5 (ads), HeyGen (avatar)
- **Voice**: ElevenLabs (podcast), OpenAI TTS (prototypes)

## Brand Voice
- Warm, informed, aspirational, deeply Brazilian but globally minded
- Portuguese (primary), English (secondary)
- Never "imigrante" — always "brasileiro no exterior"
- Never generic AI slop, clickbait, toxic positivity, cultural stereotypes

## Testing
- Every pure function gets a test
- Every API client gets a mock
- Vitest for unit tests
- Run `npm run test` before committing

## Security
- No API keys in code — `.env.local` only
- No PII in logs
- Rate limit all external API calls
- Validate webhooks with signatures
